# M11 — edge side attributes (`from=` / `to=`)
#
# An edge may request which page-space side of each node it connects to.
# Sides are page-space (as drawn): `top` is always the visual top of the
# box, whatever the diagram's or a subgraph's layout direction. The request
# is honored literally — the port lands on the requested side even when it
# contradicts the approach direction, in which case the route is routed
# around (ugly, but valid: orthogonal, never through a node).

diagram top-down

web    "Web"
api    "API"
db     "Database" : cylinder
cache  "Cache"    : cylinder
bus    "Event Bus"
queue  "Queue"
worker "Worker"

# agreeable sides: the same route the algorithm picks, made explicit
web -- from="bottom" to="top" --> api
api -- from="right" to="left" --> db
api -- from="left" to="right" --> cache

# contradictory sides: routed around, never silently reverted
api -- from="top" --> db
web -- from="top" to="bottom" --> worker

# a forced self-loop: out of the right side, around, back into the right side
worker -- from="right" to="right" --> worker

subgraph left-right "Messaging"
    bus -- from="right" to="left" --> queue
end
